{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_3wms3faq7z7ol6derxcwgoqxft4f2wkvot4zx3ou3fzmgf4rhxea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both `cargo build` and `cargo test` succeed. All 2 tests pass:\n\n- `test_tferror_to_string ... ok`\n- `test_tferror_string_and_version ... ok`\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the four `unimplemented!()` stubs in `src/tinyfseq.rs` with Rust implementations matching the C reference in `c_src/tinyfseq.h`:\n\n- **`tf_header_read`** — Validates the 32-byte buffer minimum and `PSEQ` magic, then decodes `channelDataOffset`, version bytes, `variableDataOffset`, `channelCount`, `frameCount`, frame step, compression type (lower 4 bits, validated), block count, range count, and `sequenceUid` using little-endian byte order.\n- **`tf_compression_block_read`** — Validates 8-byte minimum, decodes `firstFrameId` and `size`.\n- **`tf_var_header_read`** — Enforces `bs > 4`, decodes `size`/`id`, validates the encoded `size`, optionally copies the variable value into `vd` (when non-empty) with proper bounds checks.\n- **`tf_channel_range_read`** — Validates 6-byte minimum, decodes two 24-bit little-endian fields via a helper `tf_uint24_read`.\n\nEach function advances the `ep` end-pointer slice when provided. I added an `'a` lifetime parameter to each function so that the borrow checker accepts the `*ep = &bd[...]` assignment through the `Option<&mut &'a [u8]>`. I did not modify `src/lib.rs` or anything in `src/bin/`. The pre-existing naming-style warnings come from the original enum variants and were not introduced by these changes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2807,"cache_read_input_tokens":32535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2807,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"170c933d-c7c1-4472-